      "prompt_en": "COMPOSITION RULE, HIGHEST PRIORITY: the photograph fills the entire 16:9 frame edge to edge — never a letterbox band, never an empty panel, never a flat colour block. The bottom three-eighths of the image height — the lowest 37%, roughly the bottom 270 pixels of a 720-pixel-tall frame — contains nothing but the dark parquet floor and the table shadow running toward the camera, low in detail so overlay text stays readable on it. Every face, hand, folder, glass and chair back sits in the upper five-eighths. The table top runs across the MIDDLE of the frame, never near the bottom edge, and everything resting on it sits at mid height. Frame both men from the chest up and place their heads high in the frame. An ornate state meeting room in the Kremlin in daylight, photographed from just inside the doorway at standing height and angled very slightly down. An extremely long polished table runs away from the camera, its far end almost bare: one carafe, one glass, one closed folder. Vladimir Putin (President of Russia) sits alone at that far end, small in the frame, upper body upright, eyelids half lowered and his gaze turned to the window rather than to the papers, lips shut in one flat line, one hand laid loosely on the table edge. Much closer to the camera, standing at the side of the table in the upper left, a Russian finance official in his fifties in a dark suit holds an open folder in both hands, framed from the chest up: eyes cast down at the page, the paper edge curled where his fingers have gripped it, lower lip rolled inward, the tendons of his neck standing out. The emptiness of the table between the two men is the subject. Style: candid documentary photograph of a real place, not an advertisement, not CGI, not a composite. Shot on a full-frame camera with a 35mm lens at about f/2.8, available light from the tall windows only, true-to-life restrained colour, mild sensor noise, a slight handheld tilt, honest texture on skin, wood, paper and cloth. Ordinary room clutter belongs in the frame: a microphone stand, cable taped along the floor edge, a water tray, pushed-in chairs, worn parquet. The image stays natural — never glowing, never hyper-saturated, no HDR look, no rim-light effects, no lens flare, no arrows, no circles, no cracks, no sparks, no graphic overlays of any kind. Any lettering on the folders stays small and out of focus; exact legibility is not required. 16:9. No title overlay text, no captions, no subtitle bars, no large lettering across the frame, no watermark, no logo."
