      "concept_ko": "[모순] 강 건너 화물역은 불에 타 주저앉았는데 다리 위 대열은 그쪽에서 걸어 나온다 / [남김] 좌 2/3 사건 덩어리 대 우 1/3 인물 / 지상 눈높이 정면, 대열이 카메라 쪽으로 / 우측 가슴 위 반신 / [바꿈] 피사체(러시아 계약병 → 스무 살 남짓 북한 파병 병사) / 장소(전장 → 국경 철교) / 자세(소총 들고 행진 → 두 손으로 배낭끈을 쥔 걸음). 대본 파트 4의 「어디로 가는지도 모른 채 실려 간다 / 부대원 사십 명 중에 나 빼고 다 죽었다」가 근거.",
      "prompt_en": "COMPOSITION RULE, HIGHEST PRIORITY: the photograph fills the entire 16:9 frame edge to edge — never a letterbox band, never an empty panel, never a flat colour block. The bottom three-eighths of the image height — the lowest 37%, roughly the bottom 270 pixels of a 720-pixel-tall frame — contains nothing but the dark steel deck of the bridge running toward the camera, low in detail so overlay text stays readable on it. Every face, hand, pack strap, girder and rail sits in the upper five-eighths. Frame the men from the chest up and place their heads high, close to the top edge. A steel railway bridge over a wide border river at dusk, photographed from the middle of the deck at ground eye level so that the column walks straight toward the camera between the girders. The left two-thirds is the crossing itself: a file of North Korean soldiers in winter caps and heavy packs coming out of the far side, the nearest one sharp from the chest up and the rest smaller and hazier down the length of the bridge, and beyond them on the far bank a freight yard that has burnt — a roofless shed, a goods wagon lying on its side, blackened sleepers stacked at the water's edge. The right third is separated by a girder and its shadow: there, framed from the chest up, a North Korean soldier of about twenty grips both pack straps with his fists and walks past the camera. Eyes going somewhere past the lens without settling, heavy upper lids, lower lip caught lightly between his teeth, chin tucked back, cold-reddened ears under the cap. Cool blue river dusk with the last flat daylight on the metal, no fire in the frame — only what the fire left. Style: candid documentary photograph of a real place, not an advertisement, not CGI, not a composite. Shot on a full-frame camera with a 35mm lens at about f/2.8, ground eye level, available light only, true-to-life restrained colour, mild sensor noise, a slight handheld tilt, honest texture on skin, rusted steel, canvas and wool. Ordinary railway clutter belongs in the frame: bolt heads and rivets, peeling paint, a bent handrail, gravel ballast, a coil of wire, a hanging cable. The image stays natural — never glowing, never hyper-saturated, no HDR look, no rim-light effects, no lens flare, no arrows, no circles, no cracks, no sparks, no graphic overlays of any kind. Any lettering stays small and partly out of focus; exact legibility is not required. 16:9. No title overlay text, no captions, no subtitle bars, no large lettering across the frame, no watermark, no logo."
